# Run Away Together's ruling (CR 608.2b): "If both creatures are controlled by the same player as Run Away Together tries to resolve, both targets are illegal. The
# spell doesn't resolve." On turn 3 Bot1 casts it on its Ornithopter and Bot2's Elvish Mystic, and in response taps Old Man of the Sea to gain control of the Mystic: both are
# Bot1's as it tries to resolve, so neither goes back to a hand.

